A||N||5||2xsess||GT Wheel question||||5||
Z||000000||2xsess||09-16-2000||01:59 AM||||I'm wondering if anyone knows why the fastbacks came with the bigger tires on the back? I want to put lace GT wheels on my 85, should I just use the same size tire all the way arround? oops I just remembered that the rims are two different widths. SO I guess my question would be, should I use the same Height tires front and rear?<P>Thanks,<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT<p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 09-16-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||09-16-2000||03:29 AM||||86 and 87 GT wheels are 15" X 7" only the 88 GT/Formula wheels are different sizes. The front are 15X6 and rears are 15X7. I have 86 GT wheels on my 86 SE. I use the same size tire all around 225/50R15. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||gtsonly||09-16-2000||06:28 AM||||If I am correct, my 86 GT came with 15x7 GT rims with the rear tires being 215/60-15's and the fronts 205/60-15's. As I am to understand, the cars were set up like this to induce more understeer (push) in the car. Common with rear engine cars! So I would think by running tires of the same size you are removing what Pontiac engineered into the car. My thought!!!<P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPS<BR>http://www.fiero.nl/cgi-bin/fiero/ubbmisc.cgi||||reg||14
Z||000003||Oreif||09-16-2000||11:05 AM||||You are correct on how the GT's were originally designed. But my suspension has been redesigned by being lower and stiffer. Also larger front and rear sway bars and poly bushings. This has also correct some of the problems with the earlier suspension. Although the ride in my car is a lot stiffer it handles exceptionally well. Also my tires are wider with less roll than stock tires which attributes to a better handling car. My car is also a notchback. I don't think body design has anything to do with it but I never compared handling between notch and fastback. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||gtsonly||09-16-2000||12:43 PM||||Oh I see now oreif!! i am running stock suspension with 235/60-15's in the rear and 225/60-15's in the front. I am getting ready to put the sway bar on the rear.||||reg||10
Z||000005||gtsonly||09-16-2000||12:43 PM||||Oh I see now oreif!! i am running stock suspension with 235/60-15's in the rear and 225/60-15's in the front. I am getting ready to put the sway bar on the rear.<P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPS<BR>http://www.fiero.nl/cgi-bin/fiero/ubbmisc.cgi||||reg||10
